        "id": "ev_1",
        "kind": "pr_description",
        "label": "PR description",
        "summary": "<!-- Thank you for your contribution! -->\n\n## Change Summary\n\n`pydantic/v1/_hypothesis_plugin.py` ships with Pydantic V2. But it imported the top-level names `pydantic`, `pydantic.color` and `pydantic.types`. Under V2, those names point to the V2 modules. So the V1-only names that the module reads from them (`color.r_rgba`, `types.ConstrainedNumberMeta`, `types._DEFINED_TYPES`) raised `AttributeError` at import time. The plugin could not be imported at all.\n\nThis change points the import at the V1 namespace:\n\n    -import pydantic\n    -import pydantic.color\n    -import pydantic.types\n    +import pydantic.v1 as pyd\n...[truncated for privacy and token control]",
